==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
{{wikipedia|yes and no}}
Colloquial form of {{m|en|yea}} or {{m|en|yes}}. Compare {{m|en|nah}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/jɛː/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/jɛ(.ə)/|/jæ(.ə)/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-yeah.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-yeah-interjection.ogg|a=US|pos=interjection}}
* {{IPA|en|/jeː/|a=AU}}
* {{hyph|en|yeah}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛə|ɛ|æ|s=1}}

====Particle====
{{en-part}} {{lb|en|colloquial}}

# {{cap|yes}}.
#: {{syn|en|yes|yep|yup|aye|ya|yea|uh-huh|Thesaurus:yes}}
#: {{ux|en|&mdash;You wanna get pizza for dinner? &mdash;'''Yeah''', all right.}}
# {{n-g|Used to express [[acknowledgment]] of what was previously said.}}
#: {{ux|en|&mdash;You wanna get pizza for dinner? &mdash;'''Yeah''', I think I'm gonna have leftovers instead.}}
# {{n-g|Used to ascertain the continued [[attention]] of the listener.}}
#: {{syn|en|eh<qq:Canada>}}
#: {{ux|en|I was walking down the road, '''yeah''', and you know what I saw, '''yeah'''? A dog wearing a dress!}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The particle for ascertaining attention may be proscribed.

